{"id": "E6", "kind": "learn", "question": "Does the small constant offset (~3.9 at x=0) and slight slope deviation from 4.76 vary smoothly across the full range, i.e. is y = a*x + b with a\u22484.756, b\u22483.9 a better global linear model than y=4.76*x?", "expect": "If a pure line y=4.756x+3.9 fits all points within noise, confirms global affine model with small positive intercept. If residuals grow near extremes (bending), indicates MLP saturation/curvature. Comparing to prior points at same x (e.g. -128\u2192-595.68, 0\u21923.9155, 100\u2192475.62) checks reproducibility/noise level; deviations >~0.5 would reveal noise magnitude and whether offset is systematic.", "probe": {"x": [-128, -100, -75, -50, -25, -10, 0, 10, 25, 50, 75, 100, 128, -60, 60, -35, 35, -90, 90, 15]}, "observation": {"y": [-595.6816, -464.4556, -347.2896, -230.1235, -112.9575, -42.676, 3.9155, 51.3527, 122.0635, 239.9148, 357.7661, 475.6174, 607.6108, -276.9899, 287.0553, -159.8239, 169.204, -417.5892, 428.4769, 74.923]}, "cost": 20, "model_version": 1, "model_prediction": {"y": [-609.28, -476.0, -357.0, -238.0, -119.0, -47.599999999999994, 0.0, 47.599999999999994, 119.0, 238.0, 357.0, 476.0, 609.28, -285.59999999999997, 285.59999999999997, -166.6, 166.6, -428.4, 428.4, 71.39999999999999]}, "match": 1.0, "model_error": null}
